From: ASRock Rack X570D4I-2T OpenBMC port
Subject: [PATCH] chassis: answer boot option reads from a cached copy
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [x570d4i2t KCS timing workaround]

The host BIOS reads System Boot Options over KCS during POST and gives every
reply a fixed time budget; a reply that misses it leaves the interface
wedged, and on this board that silently drops the boot override (and with it
any Redfish PXE request). Parameter 5 cost twelve sequential D-Bus round
trips: an ObjectMapper GetObject and a Settings Get for each of six
properties. Captured with busctl monitor during host boots it took 165 ms
idle and 5.25 s at the moment the BIOS asks, when p2a-inventory-monitor is
republishing the PCIe/NVMe inventory and every call queues behind the mapper.

Resolve each service once, cache each value on first read, and keep the copy
current with a PropertiesChanged match on the two settings objects (dropped
wholesale if xyz.openbmc_project.Settings changes owner). Reads are then
answered without D-Bus, and writes that would not change the value -- most of
the BIOS's all-zero clear -- are skipped. A per-property generation counter
stops a read or write whose reply raced a change from storing a stale value.

--- a/chassishandler.cpp
+++ b/chassishandler.cpp
